 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "QKO-HROOT2: engine face to the touching CDC shell tile (one ck_ingest region, 1.667 ns): direct wires, no pin registers, so the split is cycle-exact; the native32 engine source registers its state internally"
 },
 "reset_landing": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "RTL lands eng_rst_n[1:0] at the face in 2 registered stages: each pin drives ONLY u_l0[j]; 17 kept leaves are async-reset by rst_l0[j] (equal depth, each leaf <= 32 loads); control/valid-only reset"
 },
 "structural_change": "qkd_hr_ingest_eng_sp7f (SQC-QDIE5 10-22): qkd_hr_ingest_eng_sp7d + pin_ranges ck_ingest 250-265 um on the 518.4-um W face. The qkd_hr_ingest_eng_sp7d list-order move was a no-op: route.pin_balance lays the W pins out alphabetically, so ck_ingest stayed at the SW corner (sp7b gate dump: y 1 um, pin flops eng_ddata/indata/wdata y 3-582); the range puts the entry at the pin-count-weighted middle of the 8,778 boundary sinks. sp7d (SQC-QDIE5 10-22, parallel FB to sp7c): sp6b outline height 518.4 (W pin face unchanged) and sp6b row lattice (8 rows pitch 43.2, CTS passed there at 60.7/41.3 ps spread) + sp7c ck_ingest entry pin in the W face interior; only the 3 inter-column channels that receive each SRAM's ~270-pin 20.8-um W edge are widened 24.2 -> 56.6 um (column pitch 75.6 -> 108.0), outline 475.2 -> 572.4 wide (< 600 um clock span); sp6b GRT overflow 3,915 sat in exactly those 24-um channels (hot x 150-300 / y 175-350). sp7c (SQC-QDIE5 10-22): sp7b macro lattice/outline unchanged; the ck_ingest clock entry pin moves from the SW end of the W face to the face interior (after eng_indata, ~62% of the 1,245 W pins) beside the pin-flop mass: sp7a CTS FAILED ck_ingest boundary pin-flop spread 138.4 ps > 80 TT with the entry at (0,0) and pin flops over the full 518-um face. sp6a/sp6b gate GRT congestion (sp6a 388.8x561.6 total overflow 139,692; sp6b 475.2x518.4 3,915 at 23% usage) is local: hot gcells x 150-300 / y 175-350 = the 75.6x43.2 macro lattice channels; each 32x128 SRAM has ~270 M4 pins on its 20.8-um W edge (macro OBS M1-M4), so std cells + M4 escapes crowd 24-um channels. sp7b: same source/pins/clocks, macros re-pitched: 4 columns pitch 118.8 um (67.4 um channel), 8 rows pitch 64.8 um (44 um row gap); outline 626.4x583.2 (enlarge, owner 10-21). sp6 CTS spread/timing (+91/+107 ps) were fine.",
 "slot_change_request": "UNGRANTED SPIPE6 engine slot 572.4 x 518.4 (sp6b 475.2 x 518.4); parent hr_cluster p11 repack (E-W growth only).",
 "safe_design_checklist": {
  "1_pins": "all ports on the W face touching the shell E face; ~1200 pins / 432.0 um",
  "2_reach": "engine face direct to the touching shell; internal hops < 405 um",
